  "result": "I've found the cause and written a plan, but I haven't changed any code. Plan mode is active and `ExitPlanMode` isn't available in this session, so I couldn't hand the plan over for approval.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` (`src/click/types.py:754`) returns `bound - dir`. The caller passes `dir` as the direction to move into the range: `1` for a value below min, `-1` for a value above max. Subtracting it steps outside the range whenever a bound is open.\n\n- `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-5` returns `-1` instead of `1`.\n- `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` given `10` returns `6` instead of `4`.\n\n**Fix:** change line 754 to `return bound + dir`.\n\n**Tests:** add the two cases above to `tests/test_types.py`, next to the existing clamp cases. Then run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-squishy-twilight.md`. Tell me to proceed and I'll apply the fix and the tests.",
